{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR PROFILING (verbatim, live from another session):\n\n\"Confirmed: the compaction spawns a fresh git log --full-history child every few seconds\n(7268 → 7496 …), each at ~100% CPU, holding the global write lock throughout. This is real but\npathologically slow progress on this large, long-history store.\"\n\n## Confirmed against the code, and it is the SAME BUG CLASS AS 7084 — one scale up\n\n`_compact_locked` builds the SNAPSHOT authorship ledger via\n`_build_authorship_ledger` (`compact_txn.py:72`), which calls\n`authorship.build_ticket_position_commit_map(ticket_dir)` (`attest/authorship.py:294`) —\nONE `git log --full-history` child PER TICKET, inside the store write lock. That is the\nprocess the operator is watching spawn every few seconds.\n\nThe history here is worth stating, because it is the same defect recurring at the next scale:\n- Bug 7084 / R1 found this as one full-history walk per SIGNED EVENT: measured 6.78s per event\n  on a 71,041-commit branch, 47.5s of a 48.1s compact-on-close whose real mutation is ~0.4s.\n- The fix batched it to per-TICKET: 0.53s for an 18-file ticket, 3.83s for a 159-file one.\n- That was correct for compact-on-close, which folds ONE ticket. My work made `compact-all` the\n  standing sweep, so the same call now runs once per ticket across the WHOLE store — and\n  per-ticket becomes the new per-event. At ~0.5-4s each over thousands of tickets that is tens\n  of minutes to hours of full-history walking, all of it lock-held.\n\nSo the operator's two fixes are exactly right, and I would add that fix 2's primitive ALREADY\nEXISTS:\n\n1. HOIST OUT OF THE LOCK. `git log` is read-only and never needed the write lock. Compute the\n   ledger before acquiring; then lock → re-check the ticket's event set is unchanged → stage +\n   commit → release. Identical discipline to the original P0 fix, applied one layer down.\n\n2. AMORTIZE THE WALK — and do not write a new batcher for it.\n   `authorship.build_introducing_commit_map()` (`attest/authorship.py:388`) already maps EVERY\n   tracker event path to its introducing commit in a SINGLE walk: O(events + history), measured\n   ~2s at real store scale, validated against the per-event resolver with 0 mismatches over 700\n   sampled events, and it keeps `resolve_event_commit` as a fail-closed fallback for paths it\n   misses. The sweep should build that map ONCE and query it per ticket, instead of N\n   directory-scoped walks. ~2s total in place of hours.\n\nCombined shape, as the operator put it: batch read-only prep (one walk, no lock), then short\nper-ticket or small-batch lock windows for the mutations only. That also subsumes the chunking\nfix — with the history walk gone from the critical section, the per-ticket lock window is just\nthe SNAPSHOT write, the renames and the commit, which is the ~0.4s the 7084 measurement already\nattributed to real mutation.\n\nAlso still to fix in the same pass (from the earlier field report):\n- `_commit_backfill`'s `git add -A` is unscoped and can commit a concurrent writer's in-flight\n  event files under the compactor's message.\n- `run_sweep`'s stand-aside probes `write_lock_is_busy` once before the loop, so a long sweep\n  never re-yields to writers who arrive mid-run. It should re-probe between chunks.\n\nFiling as a discovered_from ticket, NOT folding into 1733 — 1733 holds a clean LLM-Review +1\nwith zero findings and is blocked only on another session's `_config_schema.py` breach.\n\nCorroboration, unintentionally: the `rebar comment` that posted the previous field-report note\nwaited 429s for the store write lock (holder pid 57999, held 77s and counting). The stall is\nlive and I am experiencing it while writing this up."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786647341752332001,"uuid":"02949456-d14c-4385-8a25-d4f0e50cbacd"}